{
  "brand": "iolar",
  "template": "sticky-wall",
  "ratio": "3:4",
  "seed": 42,
  "series": "TERRAFORM PROVIDERS & RESOURCES",
  "date": "07/09/2026",
  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Providers: What They Actually Are",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Plugin, Not Library",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A provider is a separate binary, not linked in",
            "Core talks to it over gRPC on localhost",
            "Core owns the graph, state, plan/apply lifecycle",
            "The provider owns API calls and schema"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Core",
              "items": [
                "graph",
                "state",
                "plan/apply",
                "diff engine"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "Provider",
              "items": [
                "schema",
                "API calls",
                "validation",
                "CRUD"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Source Address Anatomy"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "terraform {",
            "  required_providers {",
            "    aws = { source = \"hashicorp/aws\",",
            "            version = \"~> 5.0\" }",
            "} }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws` = host/ns/type",
            "Short form `hashicorp/aws` assumes the registry",
            "`required_providers` is the only place to declare",
            "`provider \"aws\" {}` configures, never declares",
            "Implicit declaration guesses namespace `hashicorp`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where init Puts It"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            ".terraform/providers/",
            "  registry.terraform.io/hashicorp/aws/",
            "  5.31.0/darwin_arm64/         # os_arch",
            "# <host>/<ns>/<name>/<version>/<os_arch>"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Three Provider Families",
          "items": [
            "Managed: `aws`, `google`, `azurerm`",
            "Utility: `random`, `null`, `time`, `local`",
            "Logical: `tls`, `http`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Protocol And Timing"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Plugin protocol 5 vs 6 must match your CLI",
            "Protocol 6 needs Terraform >= 1.0",
            "Provider config is evaluated at apply time",
            "So it cannot read apply-unknown values"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Tool",
            "What it buys"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`terraform providers`",
              "full dependency tree"
            ],
            [
              "`plugin_cache_dir`",
              "no re-download per workspace"
            ],
            [
              "private registry",
              "in-house source address"
            ],
            [
              "3rd-party namespace",
              "new address, same syntax"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Safe vs Silent",
          "text": "Deleting `.terraform/` is recoverable — `init` rebuilds it. Deleting `.terraform.lock.hcl` silently allows version drift."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Resource Schema: The Contract",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Schema Is The Contract",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every resource type ships a schema",
            "A map of attribute names to types",
            "Plus behaviour flags on each attribute",
            "Flags: Required, Optional, Computed, ForceNew",
            "And Sensitive, Deprecated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Flag",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Required",
              "you must set it"
            ],
            [
              "Optional",
              "you may set it"
            ],
            [
              "Computed",
              "provider fills it"
            ],
            [
              "ForceNew",
              "change = replace"
            ],
            [
              "Sensitive",
              "redacted in plan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Optional + Computed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The tricky combo: set it, or let the API decide",
            "Omit it and the API default is recorded in state"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"b\" {",
            "  # bucket is Optional+Computed",
            "  # omit it: AWS names it, state keeps it",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Type System"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`string`, `number`, `bool` are the primitives",
            "`list(T)`, `set(T)`, `map(T)`, `object({...})`",
            "Nested blocks sit alongside typed attributes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "list(T)",
              "items": [
                "ordered",
                "index-sensitive",
                "reorder = diff"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "set(T)",
              "items": [
                "unordered",
                "deduplicated",
                "reorder = no diff"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Nested Block Modes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "single: you write the block once",
            "list: repeat it, order matters",
            "set: repeat it, order ignored"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Read The Real Schema"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform providers schema -json > s.json",
            "# machine-readable, installed providers only"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Schema is versioned per resource type",
            "State upgraders migrate old shapes on read",
            "An address is `type.name`: `aws_instance.web`",
            "The type prefix binds a provider by convention"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Plan-Time Gates",
          "items": [
            "`ValidateFunc` / framework validators run at plan",
            "They fail before any API call is made",
            "Data sources: mostly Computed, few Required lookups"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Schema Beats Docs",
          "text": "Registry docs are generated from the schema. When the two disagree, the docs are stale and the schema wins."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Arguments vs Attributes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Two Directions",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Argument",
              "items": [
                "you write it",
                "validated at plan",
                "goes in"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "Attribute",
              "items": [
                "API writes it",
                "resolved at apply",
                "comes out"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every argument reads back as an attribute",
            "Not every attribute is settable as an argument",
            "Read-only means the Computed-only ones",
            "`id`, `arn`, `private_ip`, `endpoint`, timestamps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "arn = \"arn:aws:s3:::mine\"   # config error",
            "# Can't configure a value for \"arn\":",
            "# its value will be decided automatically"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Universal id"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Every managed resource has one",
            "It is always a string",
            "It is the provider's remote identifier"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reference Is An Edge"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "resource \"aws_instance\" \"web\" {",
            "  subnet_id = aws_subnet.a.id  # reads attr",
            "}                    # and orders subnet 1st"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "One Stroke, Two Jobs",
          "text": "Referencing an attribute both fetches the value and adds a dependency edge to the graph. This is the primary ordering mechanism."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Unknown Values"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Uncreated attributes plan as `(known after apply)`",
            "Unknowns are contagious through every expression",
            "Banned in `count`, `for_each` keys, provider config",
            "That is the \"value depends on resource attributes\" error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Known Early",
          "items": [
            "Data source attributes are read at plan or refresh",
            "So they are legal inside `for_each` keys",
            "Unless the data source itself waits on an unknown"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Sensitivity Travels"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Sensitive attributes taint every expression downstream",
            "Plan output prints `(sensitive value)` instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "When depends_on Earns Its Keep",
          "text": "Only when the dependency is real but invisible to the expression graph — an IAM policy that must attach before an instance profile is used."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Meta-Arguments I: count & for_each",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Core, Not Provider",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Meta-arguments live in Terraform core",
            "They work on every resource type identically",
            "`count` and `for_each` are mutually exclusive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "resource \"aws_instance\" \"web\" {",
            "  count = 3         # web[0] .. web[2]",
            "  tags = { Name = \"web-${count.index}\" }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "resource \"aws_instance\" \"web\" {",
            "  for_each = toset([\"a\",\"b\"])  # web[\"a\"]",
            "  tags = { Name = each.key }  # = each.value",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Position vs Identity"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "count",
              "items": [
                "keys by position",
                "remove middle = shift",
                "tail is recreated"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "for_each",
              "items": [
                "keys by identity",
                "remove one = one destroy",
                "rest untouched"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The Killer Difference",
          "text": "Deleting the middle element of a `count` list shifts every index after it, so Terraform destroys and recreates the whole tail."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Choosing Between Them"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`count` for identical or on/off resources",
            "`for_each` for a keyed collection of distinct things",
            "`count = var.enabled ? 1 : 0` is the on/off idiom"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Keys Must Be Known"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "for_each keys are required at plan time",
            "Computed keys give: cannot be determined until apply",
            "`toset(var.names)` turns a list into a valid set"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "for_each = { for o in var.objs : o.name => o }",
            "# objects keyed by a stable field",
            "# here each.value is the whole object"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Addressing The Collection"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "With count: `aws_instance.web[*].id` (splat)",
            "With for_each: `values(aws_instance.web)[*].id`",
            "Over a set, `each.key == each.value`",
            "Over a map, `each.value` is the map's value"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "moved {",
            "  from = aws_instance.web[0]",
            "  to   = aws_instance.web[\"a\"]  # state only",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Migrating Safely",
          "items": [
            "count to for_each with no `moved` destroys all",
            "`moved` renames in state, zero API calls",
            "Plannable and reviewable in the diff"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Meta-Arguments II: provider, depends_on, lifecycle",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Picking An Instance",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"b\" {",
            "  provider = aws.west  # non-default instance",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Forcing Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`depends_on = [aws_iam_role_policy.p]` when no ref exists",
            "Takes references only, never strings",
            "Makes the dependent's plan more conservative",
            "More of it renders as unknown"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "create_before_destroy"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Builds the replacement before killing the old one",
            "Needed for resources behind a load balancer",
            "Needed under unique-name constraints",
            "Propagates: a dependency must adopt it too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "lifecycle {",
            "  create_before_destroy = true",
            "  ignore_changes = [tags, ami]  # drift only",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Guards And Freezes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`prevent_destroy = true` makes destroy a hard error",
            "A guardrail, not a lock — delete the block, guard gone",
            "`ignore_changes = all` freezes the whole resource",
            "Handy when adopting already-drifted infrastructure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Setting",
            "Effect"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`prevent_destroy`",
              "blocks apply"
            ],
            [
              "`ignore_changes`",
              "hides diffs"
            ],
            [
              "`replace_triggered_by`",
              "forces churn"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "lifecycle {",
            "  replace_triggered_by = [aws_instance.a.id]",
            "  precondition {        # asserted at plan",
            "    condition = var.az != \"\"",
            "    error_message = \"az required\" } }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Assertions",
          "items": [
            "`precondition` checks inputs at plan time",
            "`postcondition` checks results at apply time",
            "Both fail the run with your own message"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Literals Only"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lifecycle accepts literal expressions, no variables",
            "It is read before the graph walk happens",
            "`-replace=aws_instance.web` is the modern taint",
            "`terraform taint` is deprecated"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "ignore_changes Is Not A Default",
          "text": "It does not stop the initial create from using the argument — it only silences drift once the resource exists."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Provider Configuration & Aliases",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Default And Named",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One `provider` block = the default instance",
            "Every resource of that type uses it implicitly",
            "`alias = \"west\"` makes a second named instance",
            "Same provider, different settings"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "provider \"aws\" { alias  = \"west\"",
            "                region = \"us-west-2\" }",
            "resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"b\" {",
            "  provider = aws.west }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Passing Into Modules"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "module \"replica\" {",
            "  source    = \"./bucket\"",
            "  providers = { aws = aws.west }",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Default providers are inherited automatically",
            "Aliased ones must be passed explicitly",
            "Multi-region, multi-account, multi-cluster: same trick",
            "Multi-account usually means per-alias `assume_role`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Module Hygiene"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Child modules should not declare provider blocks",
            "One that does cannot be removed cleanly",
            "And cannot take `for_each` or `count`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "required_providers {",
            "  aws = {",
            "    source = \"hashicorp/aws\"",
            "    configuration_aliases = [aws.replica]",
            "  } }"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Missing required provider",
          "text": "`terraform init` fails with this when a module declares `configuration_aliases` and the caller never passes them in."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Credentials And Values"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Credentials come from the environment, not arguments",
            "`AWS_PROFILE`, `GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS`, never HCL literals",
            "Provider config may read variables and locals",
            "It may not read apply-computed resource attributes"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Instance-Wide Settings",
          "items": [
            "AWS `default_tags` hit every resource that instance manages",
            "`ignore_tags` stops diffing tags set elsewhere",
            "Both are per instance, aliases included"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Delete In Order",
          "text": "Removing an alias while its resources still exist leaves state you cannot plan. Destroy the resources first, then drop the alias."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Version Constraints & the Lock File",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Constraint Operators",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`=`, `!=`, `>`, `>=`, `<`, `<=`, `~>`",
            "A comma joins them as an AND conjunction",
            "`>= 5.0, < 6.0` is the explicit long form"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Written",
            "Means"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`~> 5.0`",
              ">= 5.0, < 6.0"
            ],
            [
              "`~> 5.31.0`",
              ">= 5.31.0, < 5.32.0"
            ],
            [
              "`>= 5.0`",
              "no upper bound"
            ],
            [
              "`= 5.31.0`",
              "exactly one version"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "One Segment Shorter",
          "text": "`~>` frees the last segment you wrote and pins everything left of it. Two segments buy minor freedom, three buy patch freedom."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Semver, Provider Flavour"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "major: breaking schema changes",
            "minor: new resources and arguments",
            "patch: fixes, schema unchanged"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Lock File"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`.terraform.lock.hcl` records the selected version",
            "Plus provider binary hashes: `h1:` and `zh:`",
            "Commit it — it is your `package-lock.json`",
            "`terraform init -upgrade` re-resolves and rewrites it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform providers lock \\",
            "  -platform=linux_amd64 \\",
            "  -platform=darwin_arm64  # hashes for CI"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Checksum Failure On CI",
          "text": "\"Provider produced inconsistent... checksums\" usually means the lock holds only your local platform's hashes. Add the others first."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Constraining The CLI"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`required_version = \">= 1.5\"` pins Terraform itself",
            "Separate from every provider constraint",
            "Root and module constraints are intersected",
            "An empty intersection is an `init` failure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where To Be Strict"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Reusable module",
              "items": [
                "loose: `~> 5.0`",
                "composes with siblings",
                "ships no lock file"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "Root config",
              "items": [
                "tighter range",
                "lock file committed",
                "exactness lives here"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "The Antisocial Pin",
          "items": [
            "`= 5.31.0` inside a shared module",
            "Any sibling needing 5.31.1 now fails `init`",
            "Pin in roots, constrain ranges in modules"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Resource Lifecycle: Plan, Diff, Apply",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Run, In Order",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "init",
              "refresh",
              "plan",
              "apply",
              "write state"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Plan Symbols"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Symbol",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`+`",
              "create"
            ],
            [
              "`-`",
              "destroy"
            ],
            [
              "`~`",
              "update in place"
            ],
            [
              "`-/+`",
              "destroy then create"
            ],
            [
              "`+/-`",
              "create then destroy (CBD)"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`<=` marks a data source read",
            "Replacement fires when a changed arg is ForceNew",
            "The plan prints `# forces replacement` beside it",
            "In-place when the provider has an update API call"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Refresh And Drift"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Refresh reads real state before diffing",
            "Out-of-band changes appear as a diff back to config",
            "`-refresh-only` shows drift without proposing fixes",
            "Useful for auditing, not for correcting"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "terraform plan -out=tfplan   # review this",
            "terraform apply tfplan       # apply exactly it"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Break Glass Only",
          "text": "`-target=aws_instance.web` narrows the graph for one emergency. It is not a workflow — the state it leaves never matches a full plan."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Walk Order"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Apply follows dependency order",
            "Independent nodes run in parallel, `-parallelism=10`",
            "Destroy walks the graph in reverse dependency order"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Provider Bug, Not Yours",
          "items": [
            "\"Provider produced inconsistent result after apply\"",
            "Returned state did not match the planned state",
            "File it upstream; no config change fixes it"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Adopting And Forgetting"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "import {",
            "  to = aws_s3_bucket.b",
            "  id = \"my-bucket\"   # config-driven, 1.5+",
            "}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`terraform import` does the same from the CLI",
            "Binds existing infra to an address, creates nothing",
            "Import blocks are plannable and reviewable"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "state rm Forgets, Never Deletes",
          "text": "It orphans the real infrastructure: Terraform stops tracking it and the cloud keeps billing you for it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Trade-offs, Cost, and Common Mistakes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where The Time Goes",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Provider API calls dominate wall-clock time",
            "Refresh is O(resources) network round trips",
            "A flat root module refreshes everything, every plan",
            "Split state to keep plans fast"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "plan",
              "refresh N",
              "N API calls",
              "wait"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Seven Ways To Bleed"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "What people do",
            "What it costs"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "no version constraint",
              "major bump breaks fresh init"
            ],
            [
              "lock in `.gitignore`",
              "every runner picks another version"
            ],
            [
              "`count` over names",
              "inserting one recreates the tail"
            ],
            [
              "`ignore_changes = all`",
              "real drift hidden forever"
            ],
            [
              "`-target` as routine",
              "state never matches a full plan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Provider blocks in reusable modules block module `for_each`",
            "And block clean removal of the module",
            "`depends_on` where an attribute reference is more precise"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Credentials And State"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Hardcoded credentials land in the repo",
            "And usually in state as well",
            "State stores attribute values in plaintext",
            "`sensitive` only redacts CLI output, not the file"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Encrypt The Backend",
          "text": "Passwords, keys and tokens sit in plaintext inside state. Treat the state file as exactly the secret it contains."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Trade-offs"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Many small states",
              "items": [
                "fast plans",
                "weak cross-cut refactors",
                "more wiring"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "One big state",
              "items": [
                "slow plans",
                "easy references",
                "one blast radius"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`create_before_destroy`: zero downtime, unique names needed",
            "It also doubles capacity briefly during the swap",
            "Exact pins: reproducible, but no security patches",
            "And the whole fleet drifts at once when you finally bump"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Why is my plan slow on a 400-resource root?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Refresh calls the API once per resource",
            "Parallelism hides latency, never removes calls",
            "Split into per-domain states, reference outputs"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "terraform plan -refresh=false  # audit only"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Cheap Wins",
          "items": [
            "Constrain versions in every config",
            "Commit the lock file",
            "Prefer a reference over `depends_on`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Summary: The Mental Model",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The One Split",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "compare",
          "spec": {
            "left": {
              "title": "Core",
              "items": [
                "graph",
                "state",
                "plan"
              ]
            },
            "right": {
              "title": "Provider",
              "items": [
                "schema",
                "API calls",
                "CRUD"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "gRPC between them; that split explains most behaviour",
            "Schema decides Required, Optional, Computed",
            "So schema decides argument versus attribute"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "In And Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Arguments go in, attributes come out",
            "`id` always exists on a managed resource",
            "Referencing an attribute builds the dependency edge",
            "`(known after apply)` means unknown, and unknowns spread",
            "Banned in `for_each` keys, `count`, provider config"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Five Meta-Arguments"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`count`, `for_each`, `provider`, `depends_on`, `lifecycle`",
            "Core-level and universal across resource types",
            "for_each keys by identity, count keys by position",
            "That difference causes most accidental destroys"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Address Changes Are Plannable",
          "text": "`moved` for any rename or re-key, `import` for any adoption. Both show up in the plan and get reviewed like code."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Versions, Settled"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`~> 5.0` in config sets the range",
            "`.terraform.lock.hcl` picks the point — commit it",
            "Run `terraform providers lock` before CI bites you"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Aliases In One Line",
          "items": [
            "N configured instances of one provider",
            "`provider = aws.west` on a resource",
            "`configuration_aliases` to accept them in a module"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "hcl",
          "lines": [
            "# ForceNew arg changed  =>  -/+ in the plan",
            "lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }",
            "# pair them when downtime is unacceptable"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Before You Apply"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Read the plan symbols, every single time",
            "`-out=tfplan`, then apply exactly that file"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Ship Checklist",
          "items": [
            "Source pinned, version constrained",
            "Lock committed, multi-platform hashes added",
            "No credentials in HCL",
            "No provider block in a child module"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "One Line To Keep",
          "text": "Terraform does not know your infrastructure. It knows the schema, the state, and what the provider told it last."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Terraform destroyed your whole fleet because you deleted one name from the middle of a list — that is `count` keying by position, and it is the single most expensive default in the language. This handbook walks the whole stack: providers as gRPC plugins, schemas as the contract that decides argument vs attribute, every meta-argument, and why `.terraform.lock.hcl` belongs in git. Ten pages, no filler — save it before your next `apply`.",
